s) against overall pass rate for all arms. Nano-XS is cheapest and furthest below the gate."}]}],"explore":[{"control":"The latency gate's scope (each task or all calls)","binds":"Whether any arm can be called a survivor","outcome":"Read over all calls, Brisk-S low with retry is inside the budget at {measure.latency_ms.brisk-s.low.r1.p95}. Read per task, it has no figure."}],"omitted":[{"what":"Nano-XS arms in detail","why":"They miss pass rate in every task, so they do not change the reading."},{"what":"Per-arm gate gaps for the other arms","why":"They are held in the options table and add nothing to the reading."}],"next":[{"text":"Hold per-task p95 for the Brisk-S and Atlas-M arms with high reasoning.","settles":"Whether either high-reasoning arm with retry meets the latency gate in every task."},{"text":"Re-run Brisk-S low with retry on more cases.","settles":"Whether its multi-hop and ambiguous-entity misses are real or noise."}],"method":[{"term":"Pass","text":"A trial passes by the campaign's own definition. The snapshot does not state it, so it is not described here."},{"term":"Gates","text":"Pass rate at least {criteria.pass_rate.threshold} and p95 at most {criteria.p95.threshold}, each read in every task."},{"term":"Intervals","text":"Per-task pass rates state no interval, so near misses cannot be called borderline or clear misses.","caveats":["no_control"]},{"term":"Cost","text":"Cost per 1k calls as measured. The provider routing is not named for any arm. Volume is {meta.volume_per_month} a month, and the snapshot does not say what it counts."}]}
